// pipe-parse-errors.ta — negative tests: `|>` right side must be a
// function call, a bare function name, or a constructor call. Anything
// else is a parse error. Cases below (all must be rejected by the parser,
// the first one fires):
//   5 |> 42            — int literal
//   5 |> 1 + 2         — infix expression
//   99 |> { show(7) }  — braced block (would silently drop the piped value)
//   5 |> 1.5           — float literal
//   5 |> if 1 == 1 { 2 } — special form
fn main() {
  print(5 |> 42)
}
